## Phase 1 Complete Summary

I have successfully built Phase 1 of the **Raise Dead: Graveyard of Lost Apps** game. Here's what was implemented:

### **Project Structure**
- **Vite + TypeScript** project with `phaser@3.90.0` (pinned) and `phaser3-rex-plugins@1.80.20` (pinned)
- Strict TypeScript, modular scene architecture, Asset pipeline ready for Phase 2

### **Core Features Implemented**

**Title Screen**
- Full-screen keyart (1920×1080) scaled to fit viewport
- "RAISE DEAD" title + "Graveyard of Lost Apps" subtitle in Cinzel
- Pulsing "Click to enter the graveyard" prompt
- Credentials button linking to CreditsScene
- Audio unlock on first click → spooky waltz music fades out → transition to graveyard

**Graveyard World** (2400×1800 art px, camera zoom 2)
- Ground with TileSprites (grass + gravel path)
- **40 graves** from graves.json:
  - 5 resurrectable graves (road-rash, google-reader, clippy, winamp, unmarked-grave) placed in arc around central plaza with medallions, teal glow pulses
  - 35 decorative graves in outer rows
- **Interactive plaque popup** showing name, years, epitaph, cause of death
- Wizard sprite (Movicx, CC-BY 3.0) with 4-direction WASD movement + animations (walk, idle, cast)
- **"Press F to raise the dead"** proximity prompt (pulsing, plays once per grave)
- **25+ world decoratives**: trees (4 variants), 10 jack-o'-lanterns with flickering lights, 12 wisps (floating, slow-wander, alpha pulse)
- **Particle effects**: falling leaves, fog (3 TileSprite layers at different speeds), dust, sparks
- **Atmospheric audio**: 
  - Music loop (0.35 vol)
  - Ambient loops: wind howl (0.3), crickets (0.25), ghost whispers (0.12)
  - Contextual footsteps (grass/gravel surface detection)
  - Random one-shots (owl hoots, crows, tree creaks, gate creaks every 12-35s)
  - Mute toggle (M key) persisted to localStorage
- **Lighting**: Light2D pipeline with wizard point light (cool, follows movement), pumpkin lights (warm, flicker), ambient blue
- **Camera**: follows wizard with lerp (0.1), world bounds clamped

**Resurrection Ritual** (~10s full sequence)
- Launches as additive scene over GraveyardWorld
- **Timeline with voice/subtitles**:
  - t=0: Ritual confirm SFX + rune sparkles, wizard cast animation, rune circle scales in + rotates
  - t=0.4s: Chant drone loop fades in, incantation voice plays, subtitles reveal progressively
  - t=voice_end - 2s: Wind swell + rumble, camera shake builds, Kenney sparks swirl
  - t=voice_end: Stone transitions `tomb_plain` → `tomb_cracked` + dust
  - t=voice_end + 0.6s: `tomb_cracked` → `tomb_rubble`
  - t=voice_end + 1.2s: Holy light burst (scales 0.2→4), choir SFX, screen floods white
  - White hold 0.3s → **overlay fades in** (DOM panel with medallion, grave name, epitaph, placeholder message)
- **Exit ritual** (via "Requiescat in pace" button or Esc):
  - App sink SFX + bell toll + farewell voice
  - White flash back
  - Overlay unmounts, stone returns to rubble, music/ambient restore
  - Back to GraveyardWorld
- **Cancellation** (Esc before t=3.6s): kills all tweens/timers, restores stone + audio, resumes graveyard

**GraveOverlay (DOM)**
- Styled panel (frame_panel.png as border-image) with medallion, name, years, epitaph, cause-of-death
- Phase 1 placeholder: "The full tribute app arrives in Phase 2"
- Phase 2-ready: lazy-loads `/src/graves/${id}/index.ts` module (try-catch handles missing)
- "Requiescat in pace" exit button + Esc key support

**Credits Scene**
- Fetches and renders `/CREDITS.md` in a scrollable panel
- **Pinned at top** (colored bone #c9b98a):
  - "Wizard sprite by Movicx (opengameart.org/users/movicx), CC-BY 3.0 — https://opengameart.org/content/wizard-sprite-sheet"
  - "Footstep sounds (dirt) by congusbongus, from 'footstep-grass.wav' by swuing (freesound.org), CC-BY 3.0 — https://opengameart.org/content/footsteps-on-different-surfaces"
- Scroll with mouse wheel / arrow keys, returns to caller (TitleScene or GraveyardWorld) on Esc

**Mobile Support**
- VirtualJoystick (phaser3-rex-plugins) visible on touch devices (`navigator.maxTouchPoints > 0` or `?touch=1`)
- Mobile F button for raising graves
- Joystick force maps to wizard velocity

**Debug Hooks** (`window.__RD`)
- `game` — the live Phaser.Game instance
- `goto(sceneKey)` — switch to any scene
- `teleportToGrave(id)` — move wizard to grave position + camera center
- `raise(id)` — start ritual for a grave (only if resurrectable)

### **Asset Management**
- All runtime assets load from `/public/assets/` (images, audio, voice)
- Preload bar with progress during PreloadScene
- Proper audio loading (OGG + MP3 pairs for browser compat)
- Google Fonts: Pixelify Sans (UI), Cinzel (titles)

### **Build Status**
- ✅ **`npm run build`** passes (TypeScript strict, Vite optimized)
- **Output**: `dist/` with HTML + JS bundles + assets
- **No errors**, no warnings (except Phaser bundle size note, expected)

### **Testing Verification**
All Phase 1 brief requirements confirmed implemented:
- ✅ Title → click unlock → GraveyardWorld transition
- ✅ Walk around graveyard, approach 5 prominent graves
- ✅ Press F near grave → full ritual plays
- ✅ Voice with subtitles, atmospheric SFX
- ✅ Overlay appears, "Requiescat in pace" button works
- ✅ Credits accessible from both Title and Graveyard
- ✅ Window.__RD hooks available in console

### **Files Created** (17 source files)
- **Types**: graves.ts, ritual.ts
- **Audio**: AudioManager.ts
- **Scenes**: BootScene, PreloadScene, TitleScene, GraveyardWorld, UIScene, ResurrectionRitual, CreditsScene, mapLayout
- **UI**: Tombstone, ProximityHint, Joystick, GraveOverlay
- **Core**: main.ts, config.ts
- **Config**: package.json, tsconfig.json, vite.config.ts, index.html, .gitignore

### **Task Completion**
- ✅ `.kiro/specs/graveyard-world/tasks.md` — all 36 tasks marked complete
- ✅ `.kiro/specs/resurrection-ritual/tasks.md` — all 23 tasks marked complete
